he second sumti has remained in the second place.</para>
     <para>The cmavo=20
     <quote>ve</quote> and=20
     <quote>xe</quote> switch the first and fourth sumti places, and the fi=
rst and fifth sumti places, respectively. These changes in the order of pla=
ces are known as=20
     <quote>conversions</quote>, and the=20
     <quote>se</quote>,=20
     <quote>te</quote>,=20
     <quote>ve</quote>, and=20
     <quote>xe</quote> cmavo are said to convert the selbri.</para>
     <para>More than one of these operators may be used on a given selbri a=
t one time, and in such a case they are evaluated from left to right. Howev=
er, in practice they are used one at a time, as there are better tools for =
complex manipulation of the sumti places. See=20
-    <xref linkend=3D"selbri" />for details.</para>
+    <xref linkend=3D"selbri" /> for details.</para>
     <para>The effect is similar to what in English is called the=20
     <quote>passive voice</quote>. In Lojban, the converted selbri has a ne=
w place structure that is renumbered to reflect the place reversal, thus ha=
ving effects when such a conversion is used in combination with other const=
ructs such as=20
