 <jbophrase role=3D"sumti">do</jbophrase>
 <jbophrase role=3D"sumti">mi</jbophrase>
        Who? talks to-you about-me.
        Who is talking to you about me?
 </programlisting>
     <para>The listener can reply by simply stating a sumti:</para>
     <programlisting xml:space=3D"preserve">
 <anchor xml:id=3D"c2e15d2" />
-<anchor xml:id=3D"cll_chapter2-section15-example2" />15.2) =20
+<anchor xml:id=3D"cll_chapter2-section15-example2" /> 15.2) =20
 <jbophrase role=3D"sumti">la djan.</jbophrase>
        John (is talking to you about me).
 </programlisting>
     <para>Like=20
     <quote>ko</quote>,=20
     <quote>ma</quote> can occur in any position where a sumti is allowed, =
not just in the first position:</para>
